-- Migration v19 -> v20 (named by FROM-version, per ADR 0002's sequential .sqm chain).
--
-- v20 (UC46, ADR 0034) adds **dynamic station pricing**. The mutable part of a station's economy — the
-- net signed supply/demand pressure the player accrues by trading — moves into the save behind the
-- existing StationMarket type, in a new per-slot `station_market` table:
--
--  * `station_id` — the station's PoiId slug (a TEXT key, like the reputation table's `faction_id`).
--  * `resource`   — the ResourceType NAME (stable across enum reordering, like every other resource column).
--  * `pressure`   — the net signed pressure (+ = player net-sold / oversupply / price drifts down;
--                   - = player net-bought / scarcity / price drifts up). Only NON-ZERO rows are stored;
--                   an absent (station, resource) is at base. Drift + decay are NOT stored — they are
--                   recomputed from the tick (the ADR-0007 reconstructed-on-load philosophy), so a later
--                   re-tune of the pricing constants reaches old saves for free.
--
-- A pre-UC46 save had no station_market rows, so its migrated save reads this table back EMPTY → every
-- station prices at its authored base → byte-identical to a game that never traded under dynamic pricing.
-- CREATE TABLE is supported by the bundled SQLite on minSdk-24 devices (it long predates 24), so this is
-- minSdk-safe — the same rationale as every prior additive migration. No table is rebuilt; all prior data
-- is untouched. There is NO UPSERT / NO `ON CONFLICT` — the table is rewritten as a full delete-then-insert
-- snapshot per slot (delete-all-then-insert), so additive CREATE TABLE alone suffices. Parameterized only.

CREATE TABLE station_market (
    slot_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
    station_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    resource TEXT NOT NULL,
    pressure INTEGER NOT NULL,
    PRIMARY KEY (slot_id, station_id, resource)
);

UPDATE meta SET save_version = 20 WHERE id = 0;
